---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import {
  FOUNDER_CARDS,
  cardIsActionable,
  COMMERCE_PHASE,
  FOUNDER_OFFER_OPEN,
  FOUNDER_BENEFIT_PRICE,
  FOUNDER_BENEFIT_ENTITLEMENT,
  FOUNDER_ENTITLEMENT_UNDEFINED_NOTE,
} from '../data/commerce';

const cards = FOUNDER_CARDS.map((c) => ({ ...c, actionable: cardIsActionable(c) }));
const anyActionable = cards.some((c) => c.actionable);
---

<Layout
  title="Founder access | ByteLite LLC"
  description="Founder reservations for ByteLite, Cordel Connect and Cordel Play. Nothing is charged today. Each product shows its real commercial state."
  keywords="ByteLite founder access, founder reservation, Cordel Connect, Cordel Play"
  canonical="https://www.thebytelite.com/founder-access/"
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Founder access</p>
      <h1>Reserve early. Pay nothing today.</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        Three products, three different states. None of them is finished, so none of them takes
        your money right now. This page exists so you can register interest and lock the founder
        benefit before general release &mdash; not so I can bill you for something that does not
        exist yet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Engagement map. This shows WAYS IN to ByteLite - four audiences pointing at one core. It is
       not a technology stack, not a subsystem map and not a product dependency diagram, and it
       must never be captioned as one. -->
  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <img
        class="fig"
        src="/bytelite/product-ecosystem-overview.webp"
        alt="One ByteLite core with four ways to engage: individuals, organizations, technical reviewers and founder preorder."
        width="1400" height="788" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      />
      <p class="body-note">
        Four ways in to the same thing. This is a map of how people engage with ByteLite &mdash;
        not a diagram of how anything is built.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The two benefits, kept apart. Collapsing them into "20% off" would be arithmetic on two
       different units: one is money, the other is whatever the product meters. -->
  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <img
        class="fig"
        src="/bytelite/founder-preorder-highlight.webp"
        alt="Founder preorder: 10% lower price, 10% more entitlement, reserved before general release."
        width="1400" height="788" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      />
      <h2>The founder benefit is two separate things.</h2>
      <ul class="benefits">
        <li><span class="b-num">1</span><span class="b-text">{FOUNDER_BENEFIT_PRICE}</span></li>
        <li><span class="b-num">2</span><span class="b-text">{FOUNDER_BENEFIT_ENTITLEMENT}</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="body-note">
        These do not add up to 20% off. One is a discount on the price. The other is more of
        whatever that product counts. {FOUNDER_ENTITLEMENT_UNDEFINED_NOTE}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Products.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Each card says what the thing is and what state it is actually in. Where a control is
        disabled, it is disabled because a real decision has not been made, not because the page
        is broken.
      </p>

      <div class="cards">
        {cards.map((card) => (
          <article class="card-fa">
            <h3>{card.title}</h3>
            <p class="fa-what">{card.what}</p>
            <p class="fa-state">{card.state}</p>
            <p class="fa-kind">
              {card.kind === 'reservation'
                ? 'Physical product - reservation only'
                : `Subscription - billed per ${card.interval}`}
            </p>
            <div class="fa-actions">
              {card.actionable ? (
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="btn btn-primary fa-btn"
                  data-plan={card.planKey}
                >Reserve &mdash; no charge</button>
              ) : (
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline fa-btn" disabled aria-describedby={`why-${card.planKey}`}>
                  Founder access is being configured
                </button>
              )}
              <a href={card.href} class="fa-link">What this is &rarr;</a>
            </div>
            {!card.actionable && (
              <p class="fa-why" id={`why-${card.planKey}`}>
                Disabled until its price and terms are approved. Nothing here will take a payment
                before that.
              </p>
            )}
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="fa-status" role="status" id="fa-status"></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {!anyActionable && (
    <section class="section section-alt">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <h2>Nothing is live yet.</h2>
        <p class="body">
          Every control on this page is currently switched off at the server, not just hidden. The
          commerce phase is <code>{COMMERCE_PHASE}</code> and the founder offer window is
          {FOUNDER_OFFER_OPEN ? ' open' : ' closed'}. If you want to be told when reservations
          open, <a href="/contact">say so directly</a> and I will write to you myself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>What a reservation is, and is not.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        A reservation records that you want the product and which founder offer you accepted. It
        is not a subscription, not an account, and not product access. It does not guarantee a
        launch date or a place in a queue.
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        Before anything is ever charged you will be shown the exact amount, the billing interval,
        the first charge date, how renewal works and how to cancel &mdash; and you will have to
        act to confirm it. A reservation does not turn into a payment on its own.
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        The full reservation terms are still being drafted and are not published yet. Nothing here
        can take a payment in the meantime, so there is no agreement you could enter into without
        having read them. They will be published, and you will be asked to accept them, before any
        reservation becomes a charge.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<script>
  // Progressive enhancement over real <button> elements. The browser chooses a PLAN KEY and
  // nothing else - no price, no amount, no URL - because the server reads nothing else.
  const status = document.getElementById('fa-status');
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.fa-btn[data-plan]').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const planKey = btn.dataset.plan;
      if (!planKey) return;
      btn.disabled = true;
      if (status) status.textContent = 'Opening secure checkout...';
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/checkout', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify({ planKey }),
        });
        const json = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));
        if (!res.ok || !json.url) {
          throw new Error(json.error || 'Checkout could not be started.');
        }
        // A navigation, not a form POST: the site's CSP sets form-action 'self', and widening a
        // CSP to make a payment path work is exactly what the security canon forbids.
        window.location.assign(json.url);
      } catch (err) {
        if (status) {
          status.textContent =
            err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Checkout could not be started.';
        }
        btn.disabled = false;
      }
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
.narrow { max-width: 780px; }
.page-hero { padding: 3.5rem 0 2rem; }
.fig {
  display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .75rem; background: #0d1120;
}
.hero-sub { max-width: 640px; font-size: 1.0625rem; margin-top: 1rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.8; }
h2 { margin-bottom: .75rem; }
.lede { font-size: 1.0625rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 640px; }
.body { font-size: 1rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 1rem; }
.body-note { font-size: .875rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 1rem; max-width: 640px; }

.benefits { list-style: none; margin: 1rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: .75rem; max-width: 640px; }
.benefits li {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .875rem;
  background: #0d1120; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-left: 3px solid #6366f1;
  border-radius: .5rem; padding: .875rem 1rem;
}
.b-num {
  flex-shrink: 0; width: 1.5rem; height: 1.5rem; border-radius: 50%;
  background: rgba(99,102,241,.15); color: #a5b4fc;
  display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: .8125rem; font-weight: 700;
}
.b-text { color: #e4e7f2; font-size: .9375rem; }

.cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; }
.card-fa {
  background: #0d1120; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .75rem; padding: 1.5rem;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .625rem;
}
.card-fa h3 { font-size: 1.0625rem; color: #e4e7f2; margin: 0; }
.fa-what { font-size: .9375rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
.fa-state { font-size: .875rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
.fa-kind {
  font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: #555e7a; margin: 0;
}
.fa-actions { margin-top: auto; padding-top: .75rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .625rem; align-items: flex-start; }
.fa-btn { width: 100%; justify-content: center; }
.fa-btn:disabled { opacity: .55; cursor: not-allowed; }
.fa-btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #6366f1; outline-offset: 2px; }
.fa-link { font-size: .875rem; color: #818cf8; }
.fa-link:hover, .fa-link:focus-visible { color: #a5b4fc; }
.fa-why { font-size: .8125rem; color: #555e7a; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
.fa-status { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: .9375rem; color: #a5b4fc; min-height: 1.4em; }
code { background: #131a2c; padding: .1rem .4rem; border-radius: .25rem; font-size: .875em; color: #c4c8f0; }
</style>
